<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="goals">
  <title>Course Goals</title>

  <subsection xml:id="overall-goals">
    <title>Overall Goals</title>
    <p>
      Use and understand mathematical ideas from multiple and interconnected
      perspectives, including algebraic, geometric, analytical, and numerical
      points of view. We will combine geometric visualization with careful
      analytical reasoning to solve problems and connect our ideas to other
      disciplines.
    </p>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="specific-goals">
    <title>More Specific Goals</title>
    <p>
      In MATH 13, you learned about vectors, curves and surfaces in space, and
      the partial derivatives of functions of several variables. In MATH 14, we
      will study the following topics and some of their applications.
    </p>
    <p>
      <ol>
        <li><p>Parametrization of curves and arc length</p></li>
        <li><p>Line integrals of scalar functions</p></li>
        <li><p>Vector fields, work, circulation, and flux; line integrals of vector fields</p></li>
        <li><p>Path independence, conservative fields, and potential functions</p></li>
        <li><p>Double integrals over rectangles and over general regions, and area by double integration</p></li>
        <li><p>Polar coordinates and double integrals in polar form</p></li>
        <li><p>Triple integrals in rectangular, cylindrical, and spherical coordinates</p></li>
        <li><p>Applications: mass and center of mass</p></li>
        <li><p>Substitution in multiple integrals and the Jacobian determinant</p></li>
        <li><p>Surface integrals and flux through a surface</p></li>
        <li><p>Green's theorem in the plane</p></li>
        <li><p>Stokes' theorem and the divergence theorem</p></li>
      </ol>
    </p>
  </subsection>
</section>
